/*
 * Bytestream / ByteReader — utilities for serializing and deserializing bytecode.
 *
 * ByteStream:
 *   - an extendable byte buffer used to serialize YIL structures,
 *   - supports writing u8, bool, u32, u64, i64, byte arrays, and c8 strings,
 *   - always writes integers in little-endian order,
 *   - provides direct access to the underlying buffer.
 *
 * ByteReader:
 *   - a cursor-based reader over a byte buffer,
 *   - supports reading u8, bool, c8, u32, u64, i64,
 *   - supports reading fixed-size and dynamic arrays,
 *   - performs strict bounds checking and throws MALFORMED_BYTECODE on errors.
 *
 * These utilities are used by the YIL serializer/deserializer and the bytecode
 * loader. They are intentionally minimal and allocation-free except for string
 * and array extraction.
 *
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::lint::serialize::byte
 * @File: ymirc/lint/serialize/byte.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-01-23
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
